# args: --prelude tests/checker/library-broken
# A type error in a standard-library module is an error of every program, naming the
# module, even of a program that never uses it (Jimmy, 12 November: the standard library
# always compiles). Its library is tests/checker/library-broken, whose `Broken` gives a
# `Nat` where it promises a `Text`.
# Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
One: fn Nat -> Nat
fn One n = n
